# Preserve Existing Comments

- Do not remove, shorten, or rewrite existing code comments unless the user explicitly asks for comment cleanup.
- When editing code blocks, retain nearby comments and docstrings even if they are not directly related to the change.
- Prefer minimal, targeted edits over full-block rewrites to avoid accidental comment loss.
- If a comment is clearly incorrect because of the code change, update the comment in place instead of deleting it.
- If a large refactor makes comment preservation difficult, pause and ask before removing comment context.
